			"notes": "Finds mod problems, replacing the Duplicate Mod Warning mod. Earlier versions of Mod Update Checker offer this update by themselves.\n\n- **Duplicate mods:** several copies of one mod (same file, mod id or name) are listed, keeping the highest version. Identical copies keep the one not named like a copy (`mod (1).jar`). Copies that only share a name are flagged to check first.\n- **Mods for other loaders:** Forge, NeoForge, Quilt, LiteLoader, Rift and LabyMod jars, which Ornithe never loads.\n- **Duplicate Mod Warning isn't needed any more:** if it's installed, it's offered for removal.\n- Fixing moves jars to `removed-mods` (next to `mods`), so nothing is deleted. A jar the game has open is moved when the game closes.\n- **In game:** a **Problems** tab that opens by itself on the title screen, and the menu button turns red (**Mod Problems**).\n- **Before launch:** the `--gui` window lists problems above the updates and fixes them before installing anything. `--install` moves extra copies out by itself.\n- With two copies of a mod installed, the update check now checks the copy that's kept.\n- New setting `checkModProblems` (default on), also on the OneConfig page."
		},
