			"notes": "Safer installs. Mod Update Checker 1.0.0 offers this update by itself.\n\n- **Wrong Minecraft version:** a download made for another Minecraft version (read from its `depends.minecraft`) is now refused, so a GitHub release built for e.g. 1.21 can't be installed and crash the game.\n- **Wrong loader:** Modrinth updates are only looked for on the loader the installed version was made for, so an Ornithe mod is never \"updated\" to a Legacy Fabric build.\n- **Other mods' files:** an update is refused if its file name is already taken in `mods` by a different mod, instead of overwriting that mod.\n- **Pre-launch window:** it only stays open when there's something that can be installed (updates without a file go to the launcher's log), and each update now has an **Ignore** button."
		},
